<title>ESTONIA: BALTIC 30 INDEX UP 0.5 PCT TO 101.74.</title>
<headline>BALTIC 30 INDEX UP 0.5 PCT TO 101.74.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Baltic 30 index, the only pan-Baltic index, which is compiled by the three leading business newspapers, rose by 0.5 percent to 101.74 on Thursday, Estonia's Aripaev said.</p>
<p>The Baltic 30 index covers the 10 leading stocks from the three Baltic stock markets and is compiled by Aripaev, Lithuania's Verslo Zinios and Latvia's Dienas Bizness.</p>
<p>The index was 100 on May 19 when it was launched.</p>
<p>-- Tallinn newsroom, +372 6209 201, reuters@reuters</p>
